This is a port of lha to DOS via the DJGPP development system. LHA is a
free file archiver/comressor popular in Japan. The default extention for
files produced by LHA is ".lzh". Most of the documentation of lha is in
Japanese. Brief instructions can be found in the file "lha.hlp".

This port is made from the cvs source code for "LHA for Unix" dated
20061009. The original source code can be obtained from the LHA home
site at "http://www sourceforge.jp/projects/lha". If you have trouble
getting it there, please contact me to have a copy emailed to you. The
changes to allow compiling under DJGPP have already been incorporated
into the main source, so no patch is needed.

This binary should work under plain DOS and also under Windows. It is a
command line utility, without any graphic interface. This port should
work with all of the different lha compression algorithms, including the
latest "lh7".

